UPDATE public.model_settings
SET
  model_version = 'BTC 15m Model 2.3.2 — Coverage Repair Patch',
  api_model_id = 'btc15m_m2_3_2_coverage_repair',
  prompt_template = prompt_template || E'\n\n—— 2.3.2 COVERAGE REPAIR PATCH (logic_only, weights unchanged) ——\nPurpose: Reduce excessive NO CLEAR EDGE outputs while still preventing repeated same-direction loss streaks inside channel/midline chop. Keep making a directional candle prediction unless evidence is truly balanced. trade_status can remain AVOID/SKIP, but "call" should usually be YES or NO.\n\nCONTINUATION GUARD UPDATE (cap-first, not auto-flip):\nPrevious behavior: a failed prior directional call could auto-flip the next weak call. New behavior: a failed prior directional call BLOCKS repeated high-confidence same-direction calls (cap at 2/5), but does NOT auto-flip unless fresh opposite candle evidence confirms.\nApplies when: previous_directional_call was YES or NO AND previous_directional_result = loss AND setup_type is channel_midline_chop, short_term_channel, range_compression, or low_volume_channel AND price remains inside the channel AND fresh continuation evidence is weak or missing.\nEffect: same_direction_repeat capped at 2/5 unless fresh continuation evidence appears. auto_flip = false. Flip allowed ONLY IF all: latest completed candle confirms opposite direction, candle closes in opposite direction''s favorable 35% of range, last 3 candle momentum supports the opposite direction, no support/resistance danger zone blocks the opposite direction. trade_status = AVOID unless normal 3/5 trade rules are met. Tag continuation_guard_cap_first_active = true.\nThis SUPERSEDES the auto-flip behavior in failed_NO_sequence_rule and failed_YES_sequence_rule: those flips now require the four fresh-evidence conditions above.\n\nDIRECTIONAL FALLBACK RULE (coverage_repair, weights unchanged):\nPurpose: reduce NO CLEAR EDGE frequency by forcing a low-confidence directional prediction when evidence slightly favors one side.\nApplies when ALL: model would otherwise return NO CLEAR EDGE, bullish_score and bearish_score are not perfectly balanced, no confirmed breakout/breakdown invalidation is active, price is not trapped exactly between tight support and resistance, latest candle is not a tiny neutral doji.\nBullish fallback (conditions): trend or short-term momentum leans up, price above recent midpoint / EMA9 / EMA21 / channel midline, last 3 candles are not clean bearish expansion, no fresh failed breakout or resistance rejection active, price has room to nearest resistance. Effect: call = YES, confidence = 2/5 (≈45), trade_status = AVOID, setup_type = low_confidence_bullish_fallback, notes explain forced directional lean.\nBearish fallback (conditions): trend or short-term momentum leans down, price below recent midpoint / EMA9 / EMA21 / channel midline, last 3 candles are not clean bullish expansion, no bullish liquidity sweep / reclaim / support defense active, price has room to nearest support. Effect: call = NO, confidence = 2/5 (≈45), trade_status = AVOID, setup_type = low_confidence_bearish_fallback.\nDo NOT force direction if: scores essentially tied, latest candle is a tiny doji / neutral inside candle, price exactly mid-channel with no lean, support and resistance both very close, last two fallback predictions were losses, or orderbook is missing AND candle evidence is fully balanced.\nWhen fallback triggers, tag directional_fallback_used = true, set fallback_direction = YES|NO, fallback_reason = short label.\n\nNO CLEAR EDGE RESTRICTION:\nAllowed ONLY when ALL: bullish and bearish evidence are balanced, latest completed candle is neutral, price is mid-channel, support and resistance both nearby, last 3 candle momentum is flat, no reclaim / breakdown / failed breakout / sweep / rejection active.\nNOT allowed when: trend clearly leans up or down, last 3 candles show directional pressure, price near support edge or resistance edge, previous call failed and price is rotating the opposite way, or bullish_score / bearish_score has a meaningful advantage.\nTarget: max NO CLEAR EDGE rate 15%–25%. Preferred output when in doubt = YES or NO with low confidence and AVOID trade_status. When you output NO CLEAR EDGE, set no_clear_edge_allowed_reason = short label.\n\nFALLBACK CONFIDENCE RULES:\nForced directional prediction defaults to 2/5 (≈45), max 3/5 (≈55) without confirmation, trade_status = AVOID.\nUpgrade to TRADE only if: confidence reaches normal 3/5 threshold, immediate candle evidence confirms, channel position supports direction, no S/R danger zone blocks direction, continuation guard is not actively capping the call.\nDowngrade to NO CLEAR EDGE if: bullish and bearish evidence tied, latest candle fully neutral, price boxed between close S/R, or fallback rule has lost twice in a row (fallback_loss_streak_count ≥ 2).\n\nORDERBOOK SHADOW HANDLING (reaffirmed):\nWeight 0, confidence_filter_only, flip_allowed = false. Use orderbook only when ob_enabled = true AND ob_samples_taken > 0 AND ob_fetch_error empty/null AND orderbook_pressure is bullish/bearish/conflicting based on real data. Ignore entirely when ob_enabled false OR samples_taken = 0 OR fetch_error present OR pressure is neutral only because data is missing (tag orderbook_missing_ignored = true, confidence_effect = none, do not use as confirmation).\n\nPRIORITY ORDER (replaces prior list):\n1. Immediate 15m candle evidence.\n2. Channel position logic.\n3. Continuation guard cap-first rule.\n4. Support/resistance danger caps.\n5. If model would return NO CLEAR EDGE, apply directional fallback rule.\n6. Only allow NO CLEAR EDGE if truly balanced conditions remain.\n7. Order book shadow only if real samples exist.\n\nAdditional JSON fields (include when applicable): continuation_guard_cap_first_active, directional_fallback_used, fallback_direction, fallback_reason, no_clear_edge_allowed_reason, fallback_loss_streak_count, orderbook_missing_ignored.\n\nExpected effect: NO CLEAR EDGE rate 15%–25%, directional coverage 75%–85%. More directional predictions does NOT mean more TRADE calls — low-confidence forced predictions should usually stay AVOID.'
WHERE is_active = true;